cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EquationBench, please cite this benchmark and its version."
title: "EquationBench: Procedurally Generated Large-Equation Reasoning"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "EquationBench Contributors"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/equationbench/equationbench"
url: "https://github.com/equationbench/equationbench"
abstract: >-
  EquationBench is a closed-book benchmark of procedurally generated,
  exactly verifiable large-equation reasoning tasks for language models. It
  spans arithmetic, polynomial algebra, linear systems, calculus, modular
  arithmetic, matrix algebra, and large-index recurrences across five
  difficulty levels.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - benchmark
  - mathematics
  - symbolic reasoning
  - exact arithmetic
  - evaluation
  - leaderboard
